From 8f1a4c2b6e3d0a7c5b9e2f4a1d6c8b3e9f0a2d4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drop symmetrica's eager import of sage.matrix.constructor

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [sage.matrix.constructor belongs to the unported passagemath-modules, not a real dependency of the low-level symmetrica C bindings themselves]

sage/libs/symmetrica/__init__.py eagerly imports sage.matrix.constructor
at module scope purely to "fail early" with a nicer error when the full
Sage distribution's runtime deps are missing (per its own comment);
nothing in the compiled symmetrica.pyx bindings (kostka_number,
chartafel, outerproduct_schur, etc. - all plain integer/partition
arguments, no matrices) actually calls into sage.matrix at the C level.
sage.matrix.constructor is part of the unported passagemath-modules
(pyproject.toml.m4 only lists it as the separate "modules" extra, with
an empty-string "symmetrica" extra implying no such hard dependency),
so without this patch merely doing `import sage.libs.symmetrica` - which
every consumer of the compiled extension has to do, since Python always
runs a package's __init__.py before any of its submodules - raises
ImportError on this wheel even though passagemath-modules is not declared
anywhere as a required dependency. sage.combinat.tableau, the other
"fail early" import on the line above, is left alone: its own imports
(composition/partition/subset/combinatorial_map) all resolve to the
already-live passagemath-categories, so it imports cleanly here.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 src/sage/libs/symmetrica/__init__.py | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/sage/libs/symmetrica/__init__.py b/src/sage/libs/symmetrica/__init__.py
index 1f735d7..ea72ded 100644
--- a/src/sage/libs/symmetrica/__init__.py
+++ b/src/sage/libs/symmetrica/__init__.py
@@ -4,4 +4,3 @@
 # symmetrica does not handle this well.
 
 import sage.combinat.tableau
-import sage.matrix.constructor
